<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">State Law and Order Restoration Council</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1988">1988</a>–<a href="/years/2011">2011</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as SLORC, State Peace and Development Council</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The State Law and Order Restoration Council was the military junta that seized power in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a> on 18 September 1988 after crushing the pro-democracy uprising. It renamed the country Myanmar in 1989, refused to recognise the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-league-for-democracy">National League for Democracy</a>'s victory in the 1990 election, and in 1997 renamed itself the State Peace and Development Council, which ruled until 2011.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/state-law-and-order-restoration-council.jpg" alt="State Law and Order Restoration Council" width="248" height="202" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Government of the Union of Myanmar State Law and Order Restoration Council · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:State_Seal_of_Myanmar_(1988-2011).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
